# NOTE: Assertions have been autogenerated by utils/update_mir_test_checks.py UTC_ARGS: --version 6
# RUN: llc -mtriple=haydn-unknown-elf -run-pass=machine-scheduler \
# RUN:   -verify-machineinstrs %s -o - | FileCheck %s
# RUN: llc -mtriple=haydn-unknown-elf -run-pass=machine-scheduler \
# RUN:   -debug-only=haydn-hazard-rec -verify-machineinstrs %s -o - 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DBG
# RUN: llc -mtriple=haydn-unknown-elf -start-before=machine-scheduler \
# RUN:   -stop-before=greedy -verify-machineinstrs %s -o - \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PREGREEDY
# REQUIRES: asserts

# Role: MIR — Pre-RA list-sched format feasibility + MRI port parity + three-ready rematch + SMS-HANDOFF metrics-only packability pin (pre-RA list only; no SMS.

# Pre-RA list-sched format feasibility + MRI port parity + three-ready rematch
# + SMS-HANDOFF metrics-only packability pin (pre-RA list only; no SMS
# ResourceCycle / pipeliner hooks).
#
# Contracts pinned here:
# 1. machine-scheduler reorders logical opcodes only — no private member
#    opcodes (_S0/_S1/_S2) and no FormatID stamp before RA (phase identity).
# 2. MRI classifies vreg banks: GPR32/DR64 charge the same pooled demand as
#    equivalent physregs (parity). Unknown regs (no class) stay existential.
# 3. GPR 4R2W / DR 8R3W boundaries fire on vregs (one-below / at / one-above).
#    Three independent GPR writes force multi-cycle packing (port ResMII ≥ 2
#    under 2W) even though Full has three slots — CreateTargetMIHazardRecognizer
#    IsPreRA charges PortModel; see vreg_three_writes_port_limit Hazard.
# 4. MOVE32 is dest+src (1R1W; W68.0b logical/member schema agreement — the
#    former repeated-source form is gone, so the dedup premise is moot) and
#    tied use/def (MOVT32) still charges each explicit field. Pre-RA HR uses
#    only the MI path (no identity-dedup port model).
# 5. Flexible (ADD32 Slot012) vs constrained (ST32 Slot0) keep distinct
#    FieldSlots footprints; tryAdd tracks occupancy without setDesc.
# 6. Reverse constrained→flex (ST then ADD) and flex→constrained both stay
#    logical-only; matching-frontier tryCandidate ranks without setDesc.
# 7. Three independent ready ops (ADD32 + 2×ADD64): preferred first-fit high
#    slot would lose the three-member pack, but exact matching-frontier rematch
#    keeps the cycle legal; list-sched still emits only logical opcodes.
# 8. -stop-before=greedy still has only logical opcodes.
# 9. SMS-HANDOFF metrics-only: pre-RA never emits durable BUNDLE roots. The
#    independent ADD32+XOR32+OR32 co-issue set stays logical through list-sched
#    and stop-before=greedy; pure packability oracle is unit-pinned
#    (PreRASMSHandoffPackabilityOracleSurface). Positive clone→BUNDLE handoff
#    is sibling SMS + approved expansion hook — not invented here.
#
# Sibling SMS track owns ResourceCycle / analyzeLoop ResMII fail-close / HOOK /
# HANDOFF metrics freeze / shouldUseSchedule SMSchedule wiring. Pre-RA
# SMS-RESMII + HANDOFF packability surface (exhaustive ≤3, fail-close, port
# floor, productFormsOneExactCycle) is unit-tested via HaydnPreRASchedStrategy
# pure helpers — no setDesc. AR 2R2W capacity is unit-tested (no product AR
# opcode). Three-member rematch scoreMatchingFrontier pin lives in
# HaydnHazardRecognizerTest.
# Soft-exit QoR peer: prera-format-qor-exit.ll + productSoftExitIIFloor unit
# (port+format II floors; post-RA exact-pack correlation; no HANDOFF invent).
# shouldUseSchedule stage/spill fail-close peer: pure helpers
# smsStageCountExceedsMax / smsSpillPressureExceedsLimits /
# smsShouldUseScheduleFailsClosed (unit PreRASMSShouldUseScheduleFailCloseSurface);
# list-sched here stays logical-only — no setDesc from stage/pressure metrics.
# SMS-HOOK II-wrap false-accept peer (plan §8.4 #8): product stages cycles==1;
# PreRASchedStrategy::productIIWrapFalseAcceptFailsClosed +
# smsHookRejectsIIWrapFalseAccept unit pin
# (PreRASMSHookIIWrapFalseAcceptFailClosedSurface). CreateTargetMIHazardRecognizer
# IsPreRA books linear stage-relative scoreboard, not modulo-II ResourceCycle;
# sibling SMS owns issue-time-only differential + force-iiwrap-reject lit.
# list-sched never enables multi-cycle product occupancy or setDesc from II-wrap.
# SMS/post-RA format-acceptance differential peer (plan §8.4 #7): pure
# exactTryAddProduct polarity is shared by ResourceCycle canReserve and
# post-RA / pre-RA HR CurrentCycleCandidates. PreRASchedStrategy
# productExactCanPackSequence / productFormatAcceptanceDifferentialPins +
# scoreMatchingFrontier unit pin (PreRARCHrFormatAcceptanceDifferentialSurface;
# live rematch: PreRARCHrLiveFormatAcceptanceAgreesWithPureExact). Format is
# opcode-keyed (MI ≡ desc); MOVE32 port overcount is orthogonal. Sibling SMS
# owns live ResourceCycle packing differential; list-sched never setDesc from
# format-acceptance metrics.

--- |
  define void @vreg_gpr_addi_no_member() { ret void }
  define void @vreg_move32_dedup() { ret void }
  define void @vreg_three_writes_port_limit() { ret void }
  define void @vreg_dr64_ports() { ret void }
  define void @vreg_movt32_tied() { ret void }
  define void @physreg_parity_add() { ret void }
  define void @vreg_gpr_read_limit() { ret void }
  define void @vreg_flex_add_constrained_st() { ret void }
  define void @vreg_constrained_st_flex_add() { ret void }
  define void @vreg_three_ready_rematch_add32_2xadd64() { ret void }
  define void @vreg_qual_kernel_coissue_add_xor_or() { ret void }
...
